---
import FlowShot from '../FlowShot.astro';
import FlowDetail from '../FlowDetail.astro';
import shotLongDocs from '../../../assets/flow/shots/flow-long-documents-shot.webp';
import detailParts from '../../../assets/flow/details/detail-parts.webp';
---
<section class="border-t border-border/60 bg-surface-raised/30 px-6 py-14 sm:py-20" aria-labelledby="tour-longdocs">
  <div>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="of-eyebrow" data-animate="rise">Long documents</p>
      <h3 id="tour-longdocs" class="of-display scroll-mt-28 mt-4 text-[clamp(1.85rem,3.4vw,2.75rem)]" data-animate="lead">Review the whole document. Part by part.</h3>
      <p class="of-lede mx-auto mt-5 text-left" data-animate="rise">Flow splits a long local-model run only between top-level blocks, then gives every part its own review, evidence, and receipt. Approve, decline, or skip in any order. The finish line reports exactly what you approved; everything else stays byte-for-byte unchanged.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-text-muted">Today this path runs on local models. Cloud models decline work beyond one window instead of silently cutting it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="of-stage of-stage--pad-bottom mt-12" data-animate="plate">
      <FlowShot src={shotLongDocs} alt="A multi-part Flow review with part chips, an exact coverage line, and Skip beside the approval controls." sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 78rem, (min-width: 1024px) 64rem, 100vw" />
      <FlowDetail class="of-stage__detail of-stage__detail--br" src={detailParts} alt="Flow's review header with numbered part chips and the line zero approved, zero declined, two remaining." caption="Coverage in plain counts · Approve, decline, or skip" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 30rem, (min-width: 1024px) 27rem, calc(100vw - 3rem)" glow animate />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
